<concept id="t00026">
	<title>Vehicle Identification Number (VIN)</title>
	<shortdesc>Use your Vehicle Identification Number (VIN) to register your vehicle and in all legal matters pertaining to ownership.</shortdesc>
	<prolog>
		<metadata>
			<keywords>
				<indexterm>specifications
					<indexterm>vehicle identification number (VIN)</indexterm>
				</indexterm>
				<indexterm>vehicle identification number (VIN)</indexterm>
			</keywords>
		</metadata>
	</prolog>
	<conbody>
		<table colsep="1" frame="none" outputclass="formatc_none" rowsep="1" otherprops="legalnotice_europe-general_gen-mid_2023_20230101_00005" id="e00110">
			<tgroup cols="2" colsep="0" rowsep="1">
				<colspec colname="col1" colnum="1" colsep="0" colwidth="50*"/>
				<colspec colname="col2" colnum="2" colsep="0" colwidth="50*"/>
				<tbody>
					<row rowsep="1">
						<entry colname="col1">
							<fig id="e00111">
								<title>VIN</title>
								<image href="images/N_SP3i25_D03_002_1_IR.jpg" scale="95" align="center" placement="break"/>
							</fig>
						</entry>
						<entry colname="col2"/>
					</row>
				</tbody>
			</tgroup>
		</table>
		<p>The VIN is punched into the floor underneath the passenger (or driver) seat. To check the VIN, open the cover.</p>
		<table colsep="1" frame="none" outputclass="formatc_none" rowsep="1" id="e00112">
			<tgroup cols="2" colsep="0" rowsep="1">
				<colspec colname="col1" colnum="1" colsep="0" colwidth="50*"/>
				<colspec colname="col2" colnum="2" colsep="0" colwidth="50*"/>
				<tbody>
					<row rowsep="1">
						<entry colname="col1">
							<fig id="e00113">
								<title>VIN label</title>
								<image href="images/N_SP327_D03_001.jpg" scale="95" align="center" placement="break"/>
							</fig>
						</entry>
						<entry colname="col2"/>
					</row>
				</tbody>
			</tgroup>
		</table>
		<p>The VIN is also on a plate attached to the top of the instrument panel. You can see the VIN on the plate through the windshield from outside.</p>
